# Innioasis Y1 (MT6572) thirty-fifth-boot kernel, Wi-Fi W3 (the first Wi-Fi firmware boot): allnoconfig plus exactly
# these lines (docs/planning/Y1-WIFI-PLAN.md, W3): the thirty-fourth-boot fragment with the Y2's Wi-Fi lines (cfg80211
# with the signed regulatory database; W5: AF_PACKET for wpa_supplicant and udhcpc) and the Y1's Wi-Fi option
# (CONFIG_BT_INNIOASIS_Y1_WIFI, overlays 0036/0040);
# the thirty-fourth initramfs list unchanged.
#
# Thirty-fourth-boot description, Bluetooth B6:
# (hci0, BlueZ, BlueALSA, Reborn): allnoconfig plus exactly these lines (docs/planning/Y1-BLUETOOTH-PLAN.md, B6):
# the thirty-third-boot fragment with the Y2's
# remaining Bluetooth lines (RFCOMM as the Y2, HIDP/BNEP/RFCOMM-TTY off, RFKILL, UHID, the AES/CCM ciphers SMP and
# BlueZ use; no Wi-Fi), and the initramfs with the Bluetooth service list (y1-thirty-fourth-boot.list).
#
# Thirty-third-boot description, Bluetooth B5:
# Bluetooth B5 (the WMT boot, started from userspace): allnoconfig
# plus exactly these lines (docs/planning/Y1-BLUETOOTH-PLAN.md, B5): the thirty-second-boot fragment unchanged; the
# device tree selects the "wmt" bring-up (one attempt per write to its bring_up attribute) and the firmware path.
#
# Thirty-second-boot description, Bluetooth B4:
# power on to the chip ID only, allnoconfig plus
# exactly these lines (docs/planning/Y1-BLUETOOTH-PLAN.md, B4): the thirty-first-boot fragment plus the Bluetooth
# core and the Y1 connectivity owner (CONFIG_BT_INNIOASIS_Y1, overlays 0036/0037), limited by the device tree to
# the chip-id bring-up: CONN on, the chip ID read and logged, CONN off; no firmware, no BTIF, no HCI device.
#
# Thirty-first-boot description, the radio memory reserved:
# (docs/planning/Y1-BLUETOOTH-PLAN.md, B3): the thirtieth-boot fragment with the kernel 1 MiB higher (TEXT_OFFSET
# 0x00108000, overlays 0038/0039, as stock's 0x80108000); the device tree reserves 0x80000000/1 MiB no-map for the
# connectivity core. No Bluetooth driver, no radio power.
#
# Thirtieth-boot description, power off from Reborn:
# (docs/planning/Y1-REBORN-PLAN.md): the twenty-ninth-boot fragment; a 3 s hold of the centre button also reports
# KEY_POWER (overlay 0033, switched on in the device tree), Reborn's Power.
#
# Twenty-ninth-boot description, the charging screen:
# (docs/planning/Y1-CHARGE-MODE-PLAN.md): the twenty-eighth-boot fragment; the charging screen is PID1.
#
# Twenty-eighth-boot description, the quiet boot with the splash:
# lines (docs/planning/Y1-BOOT-SPLASH-PLAN.md): the twenty-seventh-boot fragment with the twenty-eighth-boot
# initramfs (PID1's text on the serial console, reborn-splash before the services); the console level is in the
# device tree's bootargs.
#
# Twenty-seventh-boot description, MTP with the musb fix:
# (docs/planning/Y1-MTP-PLAN.md, X2): the twenty-fifth-boot fragment (MTP at boot); the fix is the overlay 0035
# (musb RX restart keeps a waiting packet). No config change.
#
# Twenty-fifth-boot description, MTP:
# (docs/planning/Y1-MTP-PLAN.md, M2): the twenty-fourth-boot fragment with the twenty-fifth-boot initramfs
# (S45y1-mtp: umtprd with /data/music); no kernel change.
#
# Twenty-fourth-boot description:
# exactly these lines (docs/planning/Y1-MTP-PLAN.md, M1 retried): the twenty-second-boot fragment (configfs gadget,
# FunctionFS, POSIX message queues, no g_cdc) with the twenty-third's PID1 (charge-only mode) as well.
#
# Twenty-second-boot description, the configfs USB gadget:
# (docs/planning/Y1-MTP-PLAN.md, stage M1): the twenty-first-boot fragment without the legacy g_cdc; PID1 builds
# ACM + ECM through configfs instead, and FunctionFS and POSIX message queues are there for umtprd (M2).
#
# Twenty-first-boot description, Y2DATA:
# (docs/planning/Y1-DATA-PLAN.md, stage B2): the twentieth-boot fragment with the twenty-first-boot initramfs
# (S03y1-data mounts Y2DATA); the eMMC write guard is the overlay 0034, switched on by the device tree.
#
# Twentieth-boot description, the power daemon:
# (docs/planning/Y1-POWER-PLAN.md, D2): the nineteenth-boot fragment with the twentieth-boot initramfs (the Y2's
# power daemon started with the Y1 battery profile and policy); no kernel change.
#
# Nineteenth-boot description, sound in Reborn:
# (docs/planning/Y1-REBORN-PLAN.md, stage R3): the eighteenth-boot fragment with the nineteenth-boot initramfs
# (the Y1 audio profile); the card and control names are device tree and the codec driver.
#
# Eighteenth-boot description, Reborn's first UI:
# (docs/planning/Y1-REBORN-PLAN.md, stage R2): the seventeenth-boot fragment with the eighteenth-boot initramfs
# (Reborn's start script and service list); the input renames are device tree.
#
# Seventeenth-boot description, the GPU:
# (docs/planning/Y1-REBORN-PLAN.md, stage R1b): the sixteenth-boot fragment plus mainline's MediaTek power
# domains (the MT6572 GPU domain only) and Lima for the Mali-400 MP1.
#
# Sixteenth-boot description, power management core:
# (docs/planning/Y1-REBORN-PLAN.md, stage R1a): the fifteenth-boot fragment plus CONFIG_PM (runtime PM in the
# existing drivers; no suspend, no power domains, no GPU), a regression boot before the GPU.
#
# Fifteenth-boot description, power-off:
# (docs/planning/Y1-POWER-PLAN.md, stage D1): the fourteenth-boot fragment plus mainline's MT6323 power-off
# driver (RTC BBPU, with the Y2's patch 0027). No RTC driver, no RGU charger path.
#
# Fourteenth-boot description, the speaker:
# (docs/planning/Y1-AUDIO-PLAN.md, stage C): the thirteenth-boot fragment; the AW87559 driver is part of
# SND_SOC_Y1_AUDIO.
#
# Thirteenth-boot description, headphone audio:
# (docs/planning/Y1-AUDIO-PLAN.md, stage B): the twelfth-boot fragment plus ALSA, ASoC, the simple card and
# the Y1 AFE and MT6323 codec drivers.
#
# Twelfth-boot description, both CPU cores:
# (docs/planning/Y1-SMP-PLAN.md): the eleventh-boot fragment with SMP for the MT6572's two Cortex-A7
# (mainline's boot-ROM entry and key; LK already powers CPU1). No hotplug, cpufreq or idle states.
#
# Eleventh-boot description, USB networking and SSH:
# (docs/planning/Y1-NETWORK-PLAN.md): the tenth-boot fragment with the CDC composite gadget (ECM + ACM)
# instead of the serial-only one, and IPv4 (no IPv6, no forwarding, no wireless).
#
# Tenth-boot description, the Y2 system milestone A:
# (docs/planning/Y1-SYSTEM-PLAN.md): the ninth-boot fragment plus local sockets (NET, UNIX; no INET, no
# network device but loopback) for syslogd and the Y2's services, and the initramfs with the Y1 overrides.
#
# Ninth-boot description, root filesystem step 1:
# (docs/planning/Y1-ROOTFS-PLAN.md): the eighth-boot fragment plus what the Y2's armhf glibc userspace
# needs from the kernel (the subset of production.config: VFP/NEON, futex, epoll and the other fd-based
# syscalls, scripts, ptys, sysctl) and the read-only mount chain (VFAT, loop, ext4, overlay on tmpfs).
#
# Eighth-boot description, backlight:
# (docs/planning/Y1-BACKLIGHT-PLAN.md): the seventh-boot fragment plus the backlight class and the
# shared MT6323 ISINK backlight driver.
#
# Seventh-boot description, display stage B:
# (docs/planning/Y1-DISPLAY-PLAN.md): the sixth-boot fragment plus the MediaTek DRM driver (MMSYS, mutex,
# OVL, RDMA, COLOR, DSI, MIPI TX), the LK-panel stub and fbdev emulation for the console. No IOMMU,
# no SMI driver, no display power domain; clk_ignore_unused stays on the command line.
#
# Sixth-boot description: the fifth-boot fragment plus /dev/mem, read by PID1 through
# PROT_READ mappings only (IO_STRICT_DEVMEM off: LK's display blocks have no Linux driver yet).
#
# Fifth-boot description (docs/planning/Y1-CHARGING-PLAN.md): The fourth-boot fragment plus the power-supply class, the MT6323
# charger with the Y1 USB budget source. (USB_GADGET_VBUS_DRAW only applies to bus-powered
# configurations; g_serial's is self-powered, kernel/y1/usb-source.c.)
CONFIG_ARCH_MULTI_V7=y
CONFIG_ARCH_MEDIATEK=y
CONFIG_AEABI=y
CONFIG_MMU=y
CONFIG_SMP=y
CONFIG_NR_CPUS=2
# CONFIG_SMP_ON_UP is not set
# CONFIG_HOTPLUG_CPU is not set
# CONFIG_HIGHMEM is not set
# CONFIG_ARM_LPAE is not set
# CONFIG_CPU_BIG_ENDIAN is not set
# CONFIG_THUMB2_KERNEL is not set
# CONFIG_ARM_VIRT_EXT is not set
# CONFIG_EFI is not set
# CONFIG_XIP_KERNEL is not set
CONFIG_AUTO_ZRELADDR=y
CONFIG_ARM_APPENDED_DTB=y
# CONFIG_ARM_ATAG_DTB_COMPAT is not set
CONFIG_KERNEL_GZIP=y
CONFIG_CMDLINE="rdinit=/init"
CONFIG_CMDLINE_FROM_BOOTLOADER=y
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-y1-thirty-fifth-boot"
# CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO is not set
CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE=y
CONFIG_EXPERT=y
CONFIG_MULTIUSER=y
CONFIG_PRINTK=y
CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME=y
CONFIG_LOG_BUF_SHIFT=17
CONFIG_BUG=y
CONFIG_KALLSYMS=y
CONFIG_TTY=y
CONFIG_VT=y
CONFIG_VT_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_MT6577=y
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_NR_UARTS=1
CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_RUNTIME_UARTS=1
# CONFIG_SERIAL_8250_DMA is not set
CONFIG_SERIAL_EARLYCON=y
CONFIG_FB=y
CONFIG_FB_SIMPLE=y
CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_WATCHDOG=y
# Feed a watchdog LK left running until PID1 opens /dev/watchdog (allnoconfig turns the default off).
CONFIG_WATCHDOG_HANDLE_BOOT_ENABLED=y
CONFIG_MEDIATEK_WATCHDOG=y
CONFIG_BINFMT_ELF=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_INITRD=y
CONFIG_INITRAMFS_SOURCE="/project/initramfs/y1-thirty-fourth-boot.list"
CONFIG_RD_GZIP=y
# CONFIG_RD_BZIP2 is not set
# CONFIG_RD_LZMA is not set
# CONFIG_RD_XZ is not set
# CONFIG_RD_LZO is not set
# CONFIG_RD_LZ4 is not set
# CONFIG_RD_ZSTD is not set
CONFIG_PROC_FS=y
CONFIG_SYSFS=y
# CONFIG_MODULES is not set
# CONFIG_SWAP is not set
# CONFIG_CMA is not set
# CONFIG_KEXEC is not set
# CONFIG_MTD is not set
# CONFIG_SPI is not set
# CONFIG_CPU_IDLE is not set
# CONFIG_CPU_FREQ is not set
# CONFIG_ARM_ARCH_TIMER is not set
CONFIG_HZ_100=y
CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_NONE=y
# CONFIG_SECURITY is not set
# CONFIG_ARM_PATCH_PHYS_VIRT is not set
CONFIG_PHYS_OFFSET=0x80000000
CONFIG_VMSPLIT_3G=y
CONFIG_PAGE_OFFSET=0xC0000000
# CONFIG_ATAGS is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_LL is not set
# CONFIG_KVM is not set
# CONFIG_Y2_PLATFORM is not set
CONFIG_MACH_MT6572=y
CONFIG_COMMON_CLK_MT6572=y
CONFIG_PINCTRL_MT6572=y
CONFIG_RESET_CONTROLLER=y
CONFIG_MTK_PMIC_WRAP=y
CONFIG_MFD_MT6397=y
CONFIG_REGULATOR=y
CONFIG_REGULATOR_MT6323=y
CONFIG_REGULATOR_FIXED_VOLTAGE=y
CONFIG_I2C=y
CONFIG_I2C_MT65XX=y
CONFIG_INPUT_EVDEV=y
CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD=y
CONFIG_KEYBOARD_MTK_PMIC=y
CONFIG_INPUT_MISC=y
CONFIG_INPUT_INNIOASIS_APT32F=y
CONFIG_BLOCK=y
CONFIG_MSDOS_PARTITION=y
CONFIG_MMC=y
CONFIG_MMC_BLOCK=y
CONFIG_MMC_MTK=y
CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT=y
# CONFIG_USB is not set
CONFIG_USB_GADGET=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_HDRC=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_GADGET=y
CONFIG_USB_MUSB_MEDIATEK=y
CONFIG_MUSB_PIO_ONLY=y
# CONFIG_USB_INVENTRA_DMA is not set
CONFIG_NOP_USB_XCEIV=y
CONFIG_GENERIC_PHY=y
CONFIG_PHY_MTK_TPHY=y
# CONFIG_USB_G_SERIAL is not set
# CONFIG_U_SERIAL_CONSOLE is not set
CONFIG_IIO=y
CONFIG_INNIOASIS_MT6323_AUXADC=y
# CONFIG_THERMAL is not set
CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
CONFIG_POWER_SUPPLY=y
CONFIG_USB_PHY=y
CONFIG_CHARGER_INNIOASIS_MT6323=y
CONFIG_DEVMEM=y
# CONFIG_IO_STRICT_DEVMEM is not set
CONFIG_DRM=y
CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y
# /dev/fb0 for the PID1 test pattern (allnoconfig leaves FB_DEVICE off; seventh boot run 2).
CONFIG_FB_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_MTK_MMSYS=y
CONFIG_DRM_MEDIATEK=y
CONFIG_PHY_MTK_MIPI_DSI=y
CONFIG_DRM_PANEL_INNIOASIS_Y1_LK=y
# CONFIG_MTK_IOMMU is not set
# CONFIG_MTK_SMI is not set
CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_CLASS_DEVICE=y
CONFIG_BACKLIGHT_INNIOASIS_MT6323=y
# The Y2 userspace is armv7 Thumb-2 glibc: allnoconfig turns Thumb user binaries off (ninth boot run 1:
# the shell died silently), and the Y2's production.config also has KUSER_HELPERS.
CONFIG_ARM_THUMB=y
CONFIG_KUSER_HELPERS=y
# The Y2's glibc userspace uses the 32-bit-time syscalls (clock_nanosleep, ppoll, ...), which allnoconfig
# leaves out: tenth boot run 2 strace, `clock_nanosleep(CLOCK_REALTIME, ...) = -1 ENOSYS`, so sleeps
# returned at once and init and crond spun. (Run 1 blamed HIGH_RES_TIMERS; it was not the cause. It stays
# off here: the periodic tick of every earlier Y1 boot is the qualified state.)
CONFIG_COMPAT_32BIT_TIME=y
# CONFIG_HIGH_RES_TIMERS is not set
CONFIG_VFP=y
CONFIG_VFPv3=y
CONFIG_NEON=y
CONFIG_FUTEX=y
CONFIG_EPOLL=y
CONFIG_SIGNALFD=y
CONFIG_TIMERFD=y
CONFIG_EVENTFD=y
CONFIG_POSIX_TIMERS=y
CONFIG_SHMEM=y
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
CONFIG_ADVISE_SYSCALLS=y
CONFIG_BINFMT_SCRIPT=y
CONFIG_FILE_LOCKING=y
CONFIG_INOTIFY_USER=y
CONFIG_PROC_SYSCTL=y
CONFIG_UNIX98_PTYS=y
CONFIG_EXT4_FS=y
CONFIG_FAT_FS=y
CONFIG_VFAT_FS=y
CONFIG_NLS_CODEPAGE_437=y
CONFIG_NLS_ISO8859_1=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV=y
CONFIG_BLK_DEV_LOOP=y
CONFIG_OVERLAY_FS=y
CONFIG_NET=y
CONFIG_UNIX=y
CONFIG_INET=y
# W5: AF_PACKET for wpa_supplicant's EAPOL and udhcpc (as the Y2)
CONFIG_PACKET=y
# CONFIG_IPV6 is not set
CONFIG_WIRELESS=y
CONFIG_CFG80211=y
CONFIG_CFG80211_REQUIRE_SIGNED_REGDB=y
CONFIG_CFG80211_USE_KERNEL_REGDB_KEYS=y
CONFIG_SOUND=y
CONFIG_SND=y
CONFIG_SND_SOC=y
CONFIG_SND_SIMPLE_CARD=y
CONFIG_SND_SOC_Y1_AUDIO=y
CONFIG_POWER_RESET=y
CONFIG_POWER_RESET_MT6323=y
CONFIG_PM=y
CONFIG_MTK_SCPSYS_PM_DOMAINS=y
CONFIG_DRM_LIMA=y
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS=y
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_ACM=y
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_ECM=y
CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_FS=y
CONFIG_POSIX_MQUEUE=y
CONFIG_MACH_MT6572_RESERVE_CONN=y
CONFIG_BT=y
CONFIG_BT_BREDR=y
CONFIG_BT_LE=y
CONFIG_BT_INNIOASIS_Y1=y
CONFIG_RFKILL=y
CONFIG_BT_RFCOMM=y
CONFIG_BT_RFCOMM_TTY=n
CONFIG_BT_HIDP=n
CONFIG_BT_BNEP=n
CONFIG_HID_SUPPORT=y
CONFIG_HID=y
CONFIG_UHID=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_SHA256=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_AES=y
CONFIG_CRYPTO_CCM=y
CONFIG_BT_INNIOASIS_Y1_WIFI=y
